  "blind": "This standpoint was composed to see what was dealt, not to survey the hall. Of the 48 bodies the museum stamped in this hall — plinths are not among them, see `inventory` — this frame holds 10 and misses 38: 21 behind the camera, 13 outside the frame, 4 in the frame but behind something solid, every one of them named under `missing`. Of the 3 of those the museum calls artifacts, this frame holds 1. 695 of the hall's 1380 floor cells can be seen AT THE FLOOR from here (50%): 40 are in the frame but under something, 645 are outside the frame. At 0.90 m, the height a body stands on rather than the floor it stands on, it is 725 of 1380 — the two differ because anything knee-high shadows the floor beside it, and `cells.hidden_by` names what stopped each ray and at what height. Measured over the hall's OWN floor, the cells a body seals included, because the walk map has those subtracted already and cannot be asked what is on top of them. The hall itself covers 84% of this frame, rasterised from its own meshes; any larger figure quoted elsewhere is the bounding BOX, which is not the hall. Every number in this sentence is counted off the `held` and `missing` lists beside it — held is placed minus missing — so the prose cannot drift from the data it describes.",
