  "method": "bodies and floor cells are the museum's OWN records (_edit_records, the segment tile, _walk_cells and _walk_erased), not an estimate; in-frame is the placed camera's frustum planes; occlusion is a physics ray (parallel to forward for an orthographic camera, which has no single viewpoint). in_frame is ALREADY net of occlusion — do not subtract hidden_behind_geometry from it, and every count here is tallied from `held` and `missing` in one place so the prose and the lists cannot disagree. The ray's own blind spot: a mesh with no collider cannot occlude it, and museum wall works and every piece of em_detail's dressing have none by contract — so a work flat on a wall never hides anything here, can itself be called visible behind a collider-less pier, and a cornice standing above a cut wall costs this measure nothing while still being in the picture. Look at the PNG before quoting it.",
